    "caption": "Sharon Stone's loan broke a jeweler's rule. Martin Katz started out selling puka shells dorm to dorm. In 1992, Sharon Stone asked to wear his jewelry to a premiere, wanting to borrow a choker and a pair of earrings. Katz thought she wanted to buy them, and told her he didn't loan jewelry. He gave in if she wore his jewelry for her magazine shoots. Many more stars soon came asking to borrow his jewelry. He has dressed more than 500 celebrities since.",
